><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: there was no clear practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="11" rect="493.227997,345.091980,677.227997,437.091980"
/></text
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251113110718+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251113110720+10'00'" name="8ad369b7-e111-457a-b720-d40185978793" page="11" coords="99.779953,426.012939,445.104248,426.012939,99.779953,414.812561,445.104248,414.812561,99.779953,415.354858,444.996582,415.354858,99.779953,404.154510,444.996582,404.154510,99.779968,404.639832,445.087677,404.638062,99.779968,393.439453,445.087677,393.437714,99.780518,393.980042,445.000458,393.980042,99.780518,382.779663,445.000458,382.779663,99.780518,383.321960,445.040710,383.321960,99.780518,372.121613,445.040710,372.121613,99.780518,372.663940,353.469421,372.663940,99.780518,361.463562,353.469421,361.463562" rect="99.429932,361.113525,445.454285,426.362976" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Results from this study suggest that stress response influences engagement, focus and&#xD;performance in team environments. Stress related hormones may influence decision-making&#xD;(</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Serpell et al., 2018b</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>), and movement quality (</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Frank et al., 2019</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>). However, this current study&#xD;adds the idea that team performance may also be affected by engagement with others. That&#xD;is, in stressful conditions communication, and by extension performance, could decline&#xD;because ability to engage in sufficient levels of information declines.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="11" rect="493.227997,334.012939,677.228027,426.012939"
/></highlight
